ufsbe — FUSE3 UFS1/UFS2 with B-epsilon tree
============================================

The fusefs kernel module must be loaded before mounting:

  # kldload fusefs

To load it at boot, add the following to /boot/loader.conf:

  fusefs_load="YES"

MOUNTING
--------

Direct invocation (most common):

  # ufsbe /dev/ada0s1a /mnt

Via mount(8) (uses the mount_ufsbe(8) wrapper):

  # mount -t ufsbe /dev/ada0s1a /mnt

Via mount_fusefs(8):

  # mount_fusefs auto /mnt ufsbe /dev/ada0s1a

To mount read-only:

  # ufsbe -o ro /dev/ada0s1a /mnt

FSTAB ENTRY
-----------

  /dev/ada0s1a  /mnt  ufsbe  rw  0  0

NOTES
-----

* The on-disk format is standard UFS2 as written by newfs(8).
  Existing UFS2 filesystems (with or without soft updates) can be
  mounted read-write without conversion.

* Soft Update Journaling (SUJ) is detected automatically from the
  superblock.  If the filesystem was not cleanly unmounted the journal
  is replayed before the mount completes.

* The B-epsilon tree block map is stored in the inode's di_extb[]
  fields (extended attribute block pointers, unused by the kernel for
  non-EA inodes).  A filesystem mounted by the kernel afterwards will
  treat those fields as zeroes and will be fully consistent; the
  B-epsilon index is simply rebuilt the next time ufsbe mounts it.

EOM
